STANDING RULE, added 9 Nov 2026 by the owner's instruction:

  THE READING RULE AND THE GATE MOVE TOGETHER.

  selftest_gate.sh's header already carries this one level down: "Kernel and selftest
  must move together." That sentence exists because solver2_jac was rebuilt on 28 Sep
  2026 with its comparison path, phrase builder and hit reporting all changed, and its
  self-test was not touched for another five weeks (REPORT 1.7).

  This is the same sentence one level up, and it went unlearned for four hours on
  9 Nov 2026. The log-READING rule above was widened from solver2_jac's two patterns to
  a format-agnostic pair at about 12:00 UTC, for a measured reason: a detection grep
  keyed to one producer's wording returns 0 for every other producer, including on a
  real hit. The publication GATE that enforces the same policy, pre_push_check.sh, kept
  the narrow pattern. At about 16:00 UTC a control force-added a log carrying a genuine
  hit -- a real banner line and a real commit=<sha256> -- and the gate returned PASS.
  Recorded as REPORT 1.10.

  Nothing had escaped. The point is that nothing had STOPPED it either, and the reason
  was not an oversight in the policy: the policy was correct and four hours old. The
  defect was that the correction was applied to the document and not to the code that
  enforces it.

  SO, WHENEVER THE READING RULE CHANGES:
    1. change pre_push_check.sh's PAT in the SAME commit, or state in that commit's
       message why it does not need changing;
    2. measure each new alternative over all tracked files BEFORE adding it, because a
       pattern that matches ordinary content blocks the repository and gets reverted,
       which is the same failure as a pattern that matches nothing;
    3. run ./shape_arm_control.sh, whose assertion 5 forces a hit-bearing file into the
       index and REQUIRES a BLOCK. Assertion 4 -- that the gate still PASSes with that
       file merely on disk -- passes either way, because the gate never looks at
       gitignored files; on its own it certified the broken gate.
    4. Both arms need a positive control, not just quiet. A check that has never been
       seen to fire is REPORT 1.7, whatever it is checking.

  The converse holds too: if the gate is widened, widen the reading rule, or say why
  not. Either one alone leaves a policy and its enforcement disagreeing, and the
  disagreement is invisible until something is actually wrong.
